# docs/NATIVE-AGENTS.md §3.3 — the amber mark: a thread that moved while you were elsewhere is
#   `needs you`, and looking at it is what clears the mark
# docs/NATIVE-AGENTS.md §6.1 — a gate is answered from the thread, and only the thread
#
# The mark only means anything if it appears without you and clears when you look, so this
# scenario leaves the tab while the turn is still streaming.
#
# The Codex thread is what makes that deterministic. Its scripted turn streams for about a
# second before it reaches the approval, where it then waits for ever, while Claude's whole turn
# is over in about 300 ms — racing a `key` round trip. The move away is a click on a process
# tab, which is local to the app and needs no daemon round trip.
#
# The margin is real but not generous: `edit-approval.json` paces its text at 10 ms a word, so
# the gate lands about 130 ms after `enter` and the click costs about 50 ms. Raising that
# transcript's `pace_ms` to 60 would make it a tenfold margin instead of a threefold one.
fixture: agents
await idle
key o
await screen == Workspace 20000

key ctrl-s A
await agents.threads[0].provider == codex 20000
assert focused == agents.composer
await idle 30000
type apply the README fix
key enter
click tabs.tab[0]
assert screen == Workspace && mode == Terminal && key_contexts[1] == Terminal

# The turn reaches its gate with nobody watching: the tab carries the mark and the attention.
await agents.threads[0].unread == true 40000
await agents.threads[0].pending_gate == permission 30000
await agents.threads[0].state == needs_you 30000
assert agents.threads[0].pending_gate == permission && agents.threads[0].state == needs_you
assert lists.tabs.rows[3].marks[0] == needs_you && lists.tabs.selected.badges[0] == pty
shot unread
dump unread

# Looking at it is what reads it. The gate is untouched — reading a thread is not answering it.
click agents.tabs.tab[3]
await agents.threads[0].unread == false 20000
await key_contexts[2] == AgentPermission 20000
assert agents.threads[0].pending_gate == permission && key_contexts[2] == AgentPermission
dump read
quit
